--[==[
NEXUS HUB — ONE-FILE EXPERIENCE DEVELOPER DASHBOARD (GUARDED LIFECYCLE)
Build: 2026-10-25-NEXUS-HUB-v1.9.2-EMBEDDED-LOGO
Install: StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts > LocalScript
Then press Play and use Insert to show/hide the menu.

This single LocalScript provides client-side developer/testing features:
- Player ESP: viewport-based labels with HP bar, highlights, boxes, tracers, skeleton, distance limit and friend/team filters
- Team recognition and team counts
- FOV circle, crosshair, target part, visibility/team checks and frame-rate-independent camera aim smoothing
- Fly, walk/jump boost, bunny hop, infinite jump and local noclip test mode
- Local lighting options, camera FOV, FPS, player selection, spectating and local teleport tests
- 12-language GUI, responsive tabs, hover animations, dashboard telemetry, diagnostic snapshots, spawn markers, low-graphics mode, built-in RAGE/LEGIT/SEMI/BALANCED/VISUALS/MOVEMENT/PERFORMANCE/DEBUG/MAP_DEV presets, named session profiles, JSON import/export, vertical HP bars

Startup displays a release-history panel and version badge (Nexus Hub v1.9.0); the same history can be reopened from Overview. The GUI includes configurable keyboard binds. ServerHop UI is included, but actual cross-server teleport requires a companion server Script in ServerScriptService; Roblox teleporting is server-authoritative.
Persistent settings across sessions require external storage; JSON export/import is provided here.
Server-authoritative invincibility and wallbang still require server weapon/gameplay integration.
]==]


